WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.480
GOOD MORNING JOHN, IT'S FRIDAY!!!

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:28.680
Hey, found a dungeon.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:31.340
So this is backstage.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:33.940
So this first room is just gross and wet

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:35.160
But then this room

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:37.000
Tinker fantasy.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:37.660
Oh, Oh

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:38.500
It's keeps going

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.300
It smells a lot like motor oil

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:41.300
and there's a canoe!

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:43.100
'Cause, you know

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.220
and then up here,

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:46.220
there's a hole *sounds concerned*

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:48.420
Don't wor-don't worry about it

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:53.560
Feel like it's necessary for me to take this opportunity to hang out in this spot

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:54.860
and talk a little bit.

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:56.140
Going on tour is a strange thing.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:57.720
You see it from the front for a long time

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:01.220
And there's something like, undeniably cool about it

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:03.100
About poeple who are up on the stage

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:05.240
like, they're PHYSICALLY lifted off the ground

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:07.240
It's less glamorous in person, but it's still cool

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:09.500
I mean... this is amazing

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:12.000
I'm pretty sure I shouldn't be down here, but it's amazing!

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.060
There are hard work elements, there are boring elements but it is an honor and a privilege

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:17.420
To be able to do this with people

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:20.140
I feel like I hear someone coming, which is terrifying to me.

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:21.340
Is it someone I know?

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:23.060
Is it a monster?

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:25.760
Is it an employee to tell me to leave?

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:27.540
Only by waiting, will we know.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:28.840
I'm scared.

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:30.100
Hello?

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:32.920
Hello?

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:35.460
the good news is i can protect myself if it comes to that!

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:37.500
*saxophone playing*

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.900
It's a saxophone monster. *sounds amused*

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:40.120
Unknown Voice: "What are you doing in the dungeon?"

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:42.100
What are you doing in the dungeon, saxophone monster?

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:43.880
Unknown Voice: Practising the saxo-

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:44.740
*loud saxophone squeak*

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:05.940
This isn't great.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:08.300
On our way to Austin and,

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:09.560
it's raining a lot

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:11.720
We gotta do a lot of this

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:13.000
To move this

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:16.120
That was a unideal driving day, luckily it was pretty short.

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:18.280
I feel like it is very easy to make people in music look cool.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.700
And it is also like financially advantageous to do it.

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:24.420
Building up an image like a brand around an artist is vital to their success

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:27.660
and it's getting to be like how everybody presents themselves on the internet, too

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:29.620
We get to show everyone our best moments and

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:32.080
cut out all of the unpleasantness

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:33.160
all of the dirt

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:35.680
And more than ever, we have ways of getting scored on our performance

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:40.800
we get instagram likes and snapchat views and pins of your special cake on pintrest

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:42.080
I worry about that

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:43.520
Because just like how in school

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.960
we start to focus on the things that are easily quantifiable.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:48.440
Maybe were gonna start to do the same thing in life.

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:50.520
I think we've always done it with dollars,

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:52.140
but now we have all these other metrics.

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:56.420
I think that might encourage us to forget about the things that maybe aren't as quantifiable,

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:58.520
but are, in the end, much more valuable.

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:00.540
Like having great poeple in your life,

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:01.840
helping take care of those people

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:03.580
doing things that you're proud of

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:05.560
regardless of the opinions of the masses

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:06.860
strengthening your communities

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:09.180
and being a part of something bigger than yourself.

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:11.080
That's just a thing that I've been thinking a lot about

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:12.840
as we drive through the country

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:14.300
which has been wonderful.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:16.540
Thank you so much to everybody who's come out to the shows

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:19.520
And John, I'll see you on tuesday.

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:22.540
I AM A GOLDEN GOD!

